/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:12:Repair a one-cell-thick colored line network by replacing singleton markers, filling short orthogonal gaps, and redirecting yellow-marked arms to the edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:13:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:14:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:15:- A rectangular grid with a dominant background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:16:- Line colors form one-cell-thick horizontal/vertical stroke fragments.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:17:- Marker colors are exactly those whose 4-connected components are all singleton pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:18:- Red singleton markers are missing line cells; yellow singleton markers are directional controls next to a line endpoint.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:19:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:20:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:21:- Assign every marker to the nearest visible line color in row/column line-of-sight, preferring an endpoint supported along that same axis.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:22:- For each line color, fill the gap between consecutive facing endpoints in a row or column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:23:- A yellow control erases the old straight arm on the far side of its endpoint and paints the same color from that endpoint through the control pixel to the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:24:- At crossings, yellow-control rays win; otherwise an original-vs-filled crossing uses the more fragmented pre-repair line color, while pure filled crossings use the lower color id.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:25:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:26:Key insight: The singleton markers identify which sparse stroke fragments belong together; after they are colored, the intended lines are the axis-aligned gaps between facing endpoints, with yellow controls flipping one arm to the marked side.
