/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:53:- bg = most common color. Several solid-colored rectangular sprites scattered on the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:54:- One sprite has a unique single-pixel marker (different color) at one corner — this is the anchor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:55:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:56:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:57:- Identify the anchor sprite (contains the marker pixel) and the remaining pieces.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:58:- Rotate the anchor so the marker pixel lands at position (0,0) of the output.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:59:- Pack all remaining pieces (allowing 90° rotations) to tile a complete rectangle with no gaps.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:60:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:61:Key insight: The lone marker pixel picks the anchor and fixes the output orientation — it must sit at the top-left corner.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:62:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:63:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:64:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:65:<reference_puzzle index="4" source="eval" puzzle_id="13e47133" lines="56-69">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:66:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:67:Fill partitioned regions with concentric colored bands derived from marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:68:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:69:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:70:- Grid partitioned into regions by wall-colored lines.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:71:- Each region has a dominant base color and a few isolated marker pixels of other colors at varying depths from the region boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:72:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:73:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:74:- For each region, read marker colors ordered by their Chebyshev distance from the boundary to build a color palette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:75:- If no marker sits on the boundary itself, the base color leads the palette.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:76:- Paint every cell with palette[distance mod palette_length], producing repeating concentric rectangular frames that radiate inward.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:77:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:78:Key insight: Each marker's depth from the boundary defines its position in the cyclic palette; the pattern then tiles inward automatically.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:79:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:80:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:81:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:82:<reference_puzzle index="5" source="eval" puzzle_id="5545f144" lines="191-207">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:83:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:84:Move a triangular sprite across the grid, consuming aligned marker pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:85:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:86:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:87:- Frames concatenated horizontally with solid divider columns; bg is most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:88:- Each frame: a triangular arrow-shaped sprite and scattered single-pixel markers, all one color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:89:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:90:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:91:- Start from the rightmost frame.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:92:- At each step, exactly one cardinal direction from the head has reachable
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:93:  markers (on a half-line: same row or column); the sprite advances to the
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:94:  nearest one.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:95:- On reaching a marker, consume it; sprite re-faces that direction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:96:- Repeat until no markers remain; output the final sprite position on a clean bg.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:97:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:98:Key insight: The triangle's tip encodes facing direction, which sets marker-consumption priority.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:99:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:100:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:101:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:102:<reference_puzzle index="6" source="eval" puzzle_id="b10624e5" lines="24-39">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:103:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:104:Replicate a motif across quadrants with scaling and reflection keyed to red anchor blocks.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:105:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:106:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:107:- Grid divided into four quadrants by a full-row and full-column divider of a single non-bg color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:108:- Each quadrant contains a red (2) square anchor block of varying size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:109:- The top-left quadrant also has a colored motif attached to its red anchor.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:110:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:111:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:112:- Use the top-left quadrant's motif as the source pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:113:- For each other quadrant, scale the motif by the ratio of that quadrant's red block size to the source red block size.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:114:- Reflect horizontally for right-side quadrants, vertically for bottom quadrants (both for bottom-right).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:115:- Align the scaled/reflected motif so its red region overlaps the target anchor, then stamp non-bg pixels.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:116:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:117:Key insight: Red block size encodes the scale factor; quadrant position encodes the reflection axes.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:118:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:119:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:120:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:121:<reference_puzzle index="7" source="eval" puzzle_id="269e22fb" lines="46-60">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:122:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:123:Complete a visible crop into the shared 20x20 binary motif in its matching orientation.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:124:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:125:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:126:- The grid is a two-color rectangular crop of one rotation/reflection of the same 20x20 motif.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:127:- One color is the motif foreground and the other color is the motif background.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:128:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:129:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:130:- Try each input color as the foreground mask.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:131:- Match that mask against every possible window in every dihedral orientation of the motif.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:132:- Repaint the uniquely matched full 20x20 motif with the matched foreground/background colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:133:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:134:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:135:- The examples are partial windows of one canonical binary pattern; the local crop is distinctive enough to identify the full orientation and offset.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:136:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:137:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:138:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:139:<reference_puzzle index="8" source="eval" puzzle_id="5961cc34" lines="8-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:140:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:141:Build a red ray network by activating blue blobs via directional green ports.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:142:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:143:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:144:- bg = most common color. Large blue blobs with adjacent green pixels marking port directions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:145:- Start marker: yellow pixel atop a short red segment at grid bottom.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:146:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:147:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:148:- Extend a ray upward from start; on hitting a blue blob, recolor it red.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:149:- Activated blobs emit thick rays through green ports until boundary or another blob.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:150:- Cascade until no new blobs are reached.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:151:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:152:Key insight: Green pixels encode ray direction and width; the network activates as a chain reaction from one start point.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:153:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:154:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:155:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:156:<reference_puzzle index="9" source="eval" puzzle_id="64efde09" lines="68-83">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:157:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:158:Copy colored control-ray ports from one rectangular sprite orientation to every matching transformed sprite.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:159:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:160:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:161:- bg is the most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:162:- Several dense 2-by-N or N-by-2 rectangular sprites are dihedral transforms of one template.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:163:- Isolated single-pixel control markers sit on rays projected outward from the dominant long edge of some sprites.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:164:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:165:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:166:- For each sprite, the active edge is the long side whose cells have the strongest same-color majority.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:167:- A control marker seen first along an outward ray from an active-edge cell assigns its color to that template cell.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:168:- On every transformed sprite, draw that assigned color outward from the corresponding active-edge cell through bg cells until blocked or out of bounds.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:169:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:170:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:171:- The marker positions are not absolute; they label cells of a shared rectangular template, then the labels follow each sprite's rotation/reflection.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:172:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:173:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:174:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:175:<reference_puzzle index="10" source="eval" puzzle_id="8f215267" lines="7-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:176:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:177:Count same-color patterns per frame and represent the tally as dots inside.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:178:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:179:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:180:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:181:- Hollow rectangular frames in various colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:182:- Small monochrome pattern sprites scattered outside frames.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:183:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:184:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:185:- Remove all small patterns from the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:186:- For each frame of color C, count how many patterns share color C.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:187:- Draw that many dots along the frame's center row, spaced by 2, starting from the right.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:188:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:189:Key insight: Frames act as tally displays — scattered same-color patterns are "absorbed" and their count is shown as interior dots.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:190:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:191:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:192:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:193:<reference_puzzle index="11" source="eval" puzzle_id="9bbf930d" lines="61-72">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:194:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:195:Move magenta particles along corridors formed by parallel colored bars.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:196:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:197:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:198:- bg=7. Particles=6 in col 0. Colored bars on even rows form corridors on odd rows.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:199:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:200:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:201:- Particle goes straight through bg cells.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:202:- When blocked by a colored cell, turns 90° into the perpendicular direction
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:203:  that has a bg cell flanked by same-color bars. Stops at grid edge or full blockage.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:204:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:205:Key insight: Same-color parallel bars define the only valid corridors, so each particle follows a deterministic local trace.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:206:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:207:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:208:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:209:<reference_puzzle index="12" source="eval" puzzle_id="89565ca0" lines="120-136">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:210:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:211:Convert each colored partitioned frame into a horizontal bar whose length is its number of enclosed regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:212:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:213:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:214:- Black background with several axis-aligned colored line drawings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:215:- The line drawings are damaged by scattered pixels of one non-background noise color and by overlaps with other drawings.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:216:- Each real drawing is a rectangular partitioned frame enclosing one or more background regions.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:217:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:218:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:219:- For each non-background color, reconstruct its horizontal and vertical wall segments from dense row/column evidence.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:220:- Count the 4-connected background regions fully enclosed by those reconstructed walls.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:221:- The color with no enclosed region is the noise/pad color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:222:- Sort drawing colors by enclosed-region count; equal counts are ordered by which reconstructed frame covers the other.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:223:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:224:Key insight:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:225:- The scattered color is not an object; it only pads the histogram, while each true object's room count is stable after rectilinear wall reconstruction.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:226:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:227:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:228:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:229:<reference_puzzle index="13" source="eval" puzzle_id="58490d8a" lines="9-21">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:230:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:231:Count colored objects and record tallies inside a legend box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:232:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:233:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:234:- A black rectangular legend box with key-color pixels in its leftmost non-black column.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:235:- Outside the box, distinct objects of each key color are scattered across the grid.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:236:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:237:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:238:- For each key color, count separate same-colored objects outside the legend box.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:239:- Output the legend box repainted: each key row gets one dot per object, spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:240:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:241:Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:242:</description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:243:</reference_puzzle>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:244:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:245:<reference_puzzle index="14" source="eval" puzzle_id="dbff022c" lines="275-288">
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:246:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:247:Fill hollow sprites' interiors using a color-palette legend on the grid edge.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:248:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:249:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:250:- bg = most common color. Several hollow sprites with distinct border colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:251:- A small 2×N or N×2 palette block sits on one grid edge; one row/column lists border colors, the other lists corresponding fill colors.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:252:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:253:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:254:- Locate the palette legend on a grid edge and read it as a border→fill color mapping.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:255:- Find enclosed bg regions (holes) inside sprites that don't touch the grid boundary.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:256:- For each hole, identify the most common adjacent border color, look it up in the palette, and fill the hole with the mapped fill color.
