/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:282:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:283:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:284:- bg = most common color.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:285:- Path color P forms a thin orthogonal network with a solid square hub (NxN).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:286:- Seed colors appear in colored regions (non-bg, non-P) adjacent to path branches.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:287:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:288:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:289:- Infer P as the non-bg color whose largest component is most network-like.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:290:- Find the largest solid k×k all-P square (the hub); exclude it from recoloring.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:291:- Recolor each path branch to the seed-region color it touches most.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:292:- Recolor the hub center pixel to the seed whose branches touch the hub most.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:293:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:294:Key insight: The hub stays uncolored; branches inherit color from adjacent seed regions by adjacency count.
