/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:352:<description>
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:353:Transmit colored tokens along wire networks, converting each to its complementary 3×3 pattern.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:354:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:355:Input structure:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:356:- bg = background. Non-bg cells form wire networks and 3×3 tokens (solid blocks or X/diagonal patterns) near wire endpoints.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:357:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:358:Rule:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:359:- Every solid 3×3 token is replaced in-place by a diamond (center + 4 cardinal neighbors).
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:360:- Each token near a wire endpoint sends its complement to the opposite endpoint: solid emits X, X emits diamond.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:361:
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:362:Key insight: Token shape cycles solid → X → diamond; wires route each complement to the far end.
/home/lixinyu/snap/a/des/seed588156842/2/prompt.md:363:</description>
